Version 1.0 · 2026-11-15

Copyright (C) 2026 Nowluma contributors

Contact: **ws675170761@gmail.com**

## 1. Definitions

1.1 **“Software”** means the source code, documentation, styles, images and other materials in this repository provided by Nowluma contributors, excluding:
- **Native Components**: `nowluma-*.node`, `nowluma-*.dll`, `nowluma-*.so` and other precompiled native files shipped with a release;
- **Third-Party Components**: code, fonts, icons, libraries and other materials carrying their own copyright notices, licenses or attribution.

1.2 **“You”** means the individual or entity exercising rights under this License.

1.3 **“Non-Commercial Purpose”** means use not aimed at commercial advantage or monetary compensation, including personal study, research, technical interoperability testing, and self-hosting without a fee. Accepting donations, reimbursements of actual costs, or free infrastructure solely to support that purpose does not by itself make the use commercial.

1.4 **“Commercial Use”** includes selling, reselling, renting, paid hosting, paid deployment or operation, bundling the Software or a Modified Version into a paid product, providing a paid service using the Software, and use in the internal business operations of a commercial entity. Any exchange of the Software for money or other commercial advantage is Commercial Use, even without a separate price.

1.5 **“Modified Version”** means a version resulting from modifying, translating, adapting, merging, splitting or otherwise creating a derivative of all or part of the Software.

1.6 **“Distribute”** means providing a copy of the Software or a Modified Version to a third party by download, mirror, installer, container image, code hosting, messaging, physical media or any other means.

## 2. Grant

Subject to full compliance with this License, Nowluma contributors grant You a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable license to:

(a) view, read and study the Software;
(b) run the Software for Non-Commercial Purposes;
(c) modify the Software for Non-Commercial Purposes to create a Modified Version;
(d) Distribute the Software or a Modified Version under Section 3.

This License grants no rights in any trademark, trade name, service mark or product name, except the attribution required by Section 3.

## 3. Conditions for Distribution

When Distributing the Software or a Modified Version, You must meet all of the following:

(a) **Non-commercial**: the Distribution and use are for Non-Commercial Purposes only; any Commercial Use requires prior written permission under Section 6.
(b) **Complete license**: include the complete text of this License with the copy, without deletion, truncation or replacement.
(c) **Retain notices**: retain all copyright, license, attribution and other proprietary notices in the Software and Third-Party Components, without removal, obscuring or alteration.
(d) **Prominent Nowluma attribution**: state prominently in the Modified Version and on its distribution page (for example, README, About page, startup banner or release notes) that the work is based on **Nowluma**, with the repository address or project homepage. Do not suggest that Nowluma contributors endorse, warrant or approve You or Your Modified Version.
(e) **Mark the Modified Version**: mark it prominently as a “Modified Version”, state the modification date, and describe the differences from the original. Do not present it as an official Nowluma release, and do not use the same version number to impersonate an official release.
(f) **Third-party and Native terms**: continue to comply with the separate licenses of Third-Party Components and the separate terms for Native Components (Section 5 and `EULA.md`). This License does not change or replace those terms.

## 4. Restrictions

Unless You obtain prior written permission under Section 6, You may not:

(a) use the Software or a Modified Version for any Commercial Use;
(b) sublicense, sell, transfer or otherwise make the Software or a Modified Version available to a third party for commercial purposes;
(c) remove, obscure, alter or falsify any copyright, attribution, license or other proprietary notice;
(d) claim that You independently authored all or the main part of the Software, or that this License covers Third-Party Components or Native Components;
(e) use the Nowluma name, marks or domains to mislead others into believing that Your version is official or endorsed;
(f) circumvent the restrictions of this License by splitting, concatenating, encoding or other means.

## 5. Native and Third-Party Components

5.1 **Native Components** are separate proprietary components and are not licensed under this License. You may run the Native Components shipped with the Software only in compliance with `EULA.md` and applicable law. You may not reverse engineer, decompile, modify, copy, separately Distribute or sublicense Native Components, except where mandatory law permits and cannot be excluded by contract.

5.2 **Third-Party Components** remain governed by their own licenses. This License does not relicense, change or replace third-party licenses; if this License conflicts with a third-party license, that third-party license governs that component. You must retain third-party licenses and attribution when Distributing.

5.3 This License grants no rights in the trademarks, services or data of Tencent, QQ or any other third party. Your use of the QQ client, accounts, networks and third-party services remains subject to their terms and the law.

## 6. Commercial Use and Additional Permission

Commercial Use, or any use beyond what this License expressly permits (including Distribution that violates Section 3), requires prior written permission from Nowluma contributors. Send requests to **ws675170761@gmail.com**, stating the entity, purpose, scope, term and distribution method. A separate permission is valid only for the entity, purpose, scope and term it expressly states; it does not authorize anyone else and does not change this License for unauthorized acts.

## 7. No Warranty

The Software is provided “AS IS” and “AS AVAILABLE”, without any express or implied warranty, including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, non-infringement, freedom from errors, uninterrupted operation or security. You bear the entire risk of using the Software, including risks related to accounts, data, networks, credentials and third-party services.

## 8. Limitation of Liability

To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, Nowluma contributors are not liable for any direct, indirect, incidental, special, punitive or consequential damages arising from the Software or this License, including account restriction or suspension, data loss, lost profits, business interruption, device damage or third-party claims.

This Section does not exclude or limit liability that mandatory law prohibits from being excluded or limited. If mandatory law (for example, consumer protection law) gives You rights that cannot be waived, this License does not exclude those rights, and this Section is interpreted as required by law.

## 9. Termination and Reinstatement

9.1 Your rights under this License terminate automatically if You breach any term.

9.2 After You stop all breaches and notify **ws675170761@gmail.com** in writing, Your rights may be reinstated from the date of notice unless Nowluma contributors expressly refuse within a reasonable period. Reinstatement does not affect claims for breaches before reinstatement.

9.3 On termination, Sections 3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 10, 11 and any other provisions that by their nature should survive remain in effect.

